<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="container article-body">

    <p>Check each item that is genuinely true for your organisation right now, not what was true when the policy was first adopted. The result is a quick self-assessment, not a compliance certificate.</p>

    <div class="tool-panel">
      <div id="posh-checklist">
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p1" data-weight="1">
          <label for="p1">Our organisation has 10 or more employees and has constituted an Internal Committee (IC).<span class="checklist-hint">Below 10 employees, complaints route to the government-constituted Local Committee instead.</span></label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p2" data-weight="1">
          <label for="p2">The IC's Presiding Officer is a senior woman employee.</label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p3" data-weight="1">
          <label for="p3">The IC has at least two internal members committed to the cause of women or with relevant experience.</label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p4" data-weight="1.5">
          <label for="p4">The IC has an external member from an NGO or association familiar with sexual harassment issues.<span class="checklist-hint">The most commonly missed requirement — an IC without this member is not validly constituted.</span></label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p5" data-weight="1">
          <label for="p5">No IC member's three-year term has lapsed without reconstitution.</label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p6" data-weight="1">
          <label for="p6">Our most recent annual report was actually filed with the District Officer.<span class="checklist-hint">Separate from any board-report POSH disclosure under the Companies Act.</span></label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p7" data-weight="1">
          <label for="p7">General POSH awareness training was conducted for the existing workforce in the last 12 months — not only at onboarding.</label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p8" data-weight="0.75">
          <label for="p8">IC members themselves have been trained on inquiry procedure, timelines and confidentiality obligations.</label>
        </div>
        <div class="checklist-item">
          <input type="checkbox" id="p9" data-weight="0.75">
          <label for="p9">Our policy document reflects the IC's actual, current composition — not a stale version from an earlier year.</label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="posh-score" class="checklist-score" style="display:none">
        <b id="posh-score-num">0/9</b>
        <span id="posh-score-text"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2>Why each of these matters</h2>
    <p>These nine points map directly onto the operational requirements of the POSH Act, 2013 that sit behind the policy document most organisations already have — inquiry timelines (90 days to inquire, 10 days to report, 60 days for the employer to act), the external member requirement, reconstitution before terms lapse, and ongoing rather than one-time training. Read the full context in <a href="/legal-insights/posh-compliance-beyond-the-policy/">POSH compliance beyond the policy document</a>.</p>

    <p class="mt-32" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--text-muted);border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding-top:24px">This tool is a self-assessment aid only and does not constitute legal advice, an audit, or a compliance certification. A "compliant" result here does not confirm actual legal compliance for your organisation. For a formal POSH compliance review, <a href="/contact/">contact the chambers</a>.</p>
  </div>
